    SystemData.cpp, main.cpp, NetworkThread.cpp, ThreadedHasher.cpp: the startup index runs without the splash screen, and again when the link comes up (fork #183)
    
    INDEX NEW GAMES AT STARTUP (and the netplay index at startup) were started
    by SystemData::loadConfig only when it was handed a window, and main hands
    it one only for the splash screen's progress. ROCKNIX starts the interface
    with --no-splash, so on its devices the setting never did anything: six
    boots of the sixth candidate with the setting on, the account in and the
    link up logged no hasher line at all. The block becomes
    SystemData::startIndexesAtStart(window); loadConfig calls it as before when
    it has a window, main calls it when it gave loadConfig none.
    
    A handheld's Wi-Fi is often still associating when the interface starts, and
    a run without RetroAchievements' hash library indexes nothing and said
    nothing. The run says so now (one WARNING line), remembers whether the
    library came this session, and the network watcher starts the achievements
    half again at link-up until it has -- D-RA-013's promise that a game added
    later is cached when the device is next connected rests on the index knowing
    the game. The once-a-day stamp of the lookups-alone pass is written only
    when the library came, as its comment already promised.
    
